      "type": "引用",
      "type_label": "引用",
      "text": "So do I",
      "quote": {
        "author": "Teslaconomics",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1882967991362727936/bySD-Rwj_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-24 13:14:34",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-24T05:14:34.000Z",
        "id": "2113861688370073898",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVXyAK7bsAAdDXG.jpg?name=small"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "height": 1653,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVXyAK7bsAAdDXG.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1320
          }
        ],
        "name": "Teslaconomics",
        "text": "I trust Grok Bot with ALL my finances. \n\nNow, all 5 of my credit cards are saved in the vault.\n\nPeople think I’m crazy to do so... but if you think about it, people hand their credit card to a random waiter all the time and watch it disappear into the back. \n\nFor me, I'd rather have mine secured by the smartest AI in the world.\n\nThis is why I do it. \n\n1/ One text to buy anything. I bought my kids 2 Garmin watches, a DribbleUp smart ball and an Ollyball without ever opening a website.\n\n2/ Flights and hotels booked for me. No digging for a card, no typing numbers into 6 checkout pages.\n\n3/ Amazon orders handled with one text.\n\n4/ I just say \"put it on the United card\" or \"use the Apple Card\" and it does.\n\nFYI the bot never sees the full number or the security code. It securely remembers them, and I specifically approve what gets bought.\n\nOnce, you add your cards once, you’ll never have to pull out your wallet again.\n\nThis is how everyone is going to live soon imo.",
        "url": "https://x.com/Teslaconomics/status/2113861688370073898",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
